  "text": "proprium.sacratissimi-cordis-iesu-evangelium",
  "about": "The Gospel of the feast of the Most Sacred Heart of Jesus, John 19:31–37. A soldier opens the side of the dead Christ with a lance, and blood and water immediately flow forth.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, the Jews, because it was the Preparation day, so that the bodies might not remain upon the cross on the Sabbath—for that Sabbath was a great day—asked Pilate that their legs might be broken and that the bodies might be taken away.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w009", "w010"], "anchor": "w010", "gloss": "might not remain" }] },
    "s02": { "translation": "The soldiers therefore came, and they broke the legs of the first and of the other who had been crucified with Him.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w040", "w041"], "anchor": "w040", "gloss": "had been crucified" }] },
    "s03": { "translation": "But when they had come to Jesus and saw Him already dead, they did not break His legs; but one of the soldiers opened His side with a lance, and immediately there came out blood and water.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w054", "w055"], "anchor": "w054", "gloss": "did not break" }] },
    "s04": { "translation": "And he who saw it has borne witness, and his testimony is true. And he knows that he speaks the truth, so that you also may believe.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w074", "w075"], "anchor": "w074", "gloss": "has borne witness" }] },
    "s05": { "translation": "For these things happened so that the Scripture might be fulfilled: You shall not break a bone of His. And again another Scripture says: They will look on Him whom they pierced.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w091", "w092"], "anchor": "w091", "gloss": "were done" }, { "words": ["w099", "w100"], "anchor": "w099", "gloss": "you shall not break" }] }
  },
